          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Attention-Based Sequence Transduction with Residual Scaling"
            }
          ],
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.355,
            0.147,
            0.478,
            0.165
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Alice Nguyen"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "∗",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.549,
            0.146,
            0.65,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Bob Smith†"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.417,
            0.177,
            0.582,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "November 18, 2026"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.09,
            0.222,
            0.196,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Abstract"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.087,
            0.254,
            0.495,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We propose a simple network architecture based solely on attention mechanisms. Experiments on two translation tasks show that our model achieves 28.4 BLEU on English-to-German, improving over the best existing results by 2.0 BLEU, while requiring significantly less time to train."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.089,
            0.371,
            0.276,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1 Introduction"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.087,
            0.403,
            0.494,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Recurrent networks [4] have been the dominant approach. In this work we show that attention alone suffices."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.089,
            0.474,
            0.222,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2 Method"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.088,
            0.505,
            0.493,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Given an input sequence "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = (x_{1},\\dots ,x_{n})"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " with "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x_{i}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we compute queries "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "Q = XW^{Q}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , keys "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "K = XW^{K}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and values "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "V = XW^{V}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "W^{Q}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d\\times d_{k}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . The scaled dotproduct attention is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.578,
            0.491,
            0.613
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "\\text {Attention} (Q, K, V) = \\text {softmax} \\left(\\frac {Q K ^ {\\top}}{\\sqrt {d _ {k}}}\\right) V.\\tag{1}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.088,
            0.625,
            0.493,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As shown in Eq. (1) , the factor "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 / \\sqrt{d_k}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " prevents the softmax from saturating when "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "d_{k}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is large, e.g. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "d_{k} = 64"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Following [1, 2], we add residual connections so that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = x + f(x)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and the loss is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.698,
            0.491,
            0.74
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathcal {L} (\\theta) = - \\frac {1}{N} \\sum_ {i = 1} ^ {N} \\log p _ {\\theta} (y _ {i} \\mid x _ {i}) + \\lambda \\| \\theta \\| _ {2} ^ {2},\\tag{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.087,
            0.752,
            0.488,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "with "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\lambda = 0.01"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . The learning rate follows "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\eta_t = d^{-0.5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " min "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(t^{-0.5}, t \\cdot w^{-1.5})"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for warmup "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w = 4000"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " steps."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.089,
            0.809,
            0.277,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3 Experiments"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.088,
            0.84,
            0.494,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We train on WMT 2014 English–German, which contains about 4.5 million sentence pairs, and report BLEU"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.555,
            0.252,
            0.861,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_caption",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.505,
                0.234,
                0.908,
                0.25
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Table 1: BLEU scores and training cost on newstest2014."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 17,
              "bbox": [
                0.555,
                0.252,
                0.861,
                0.36
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_table_17.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">Model</td><td rowspan=\"2\">Size</td><td colspan=\"2\">BLEU</td></tr><tr><td>EN-DE</td><td>EN-FR</td></tr><tr><td>ByteNet</td><td>1.2B</td><td>23.75</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>ConvS2S</td><td>0.9B</td><td>25.16</td><td>40.46</td></tr><tr><td>Ours (base)</td><td>65M</td><td>27.3</td><td>38.1</td></tr><tr><td>Ours (big)</td><td>213M</td><td>28.4</td><td>41.8</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.545,
            0.378,
            0.874,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "chart_body",
              "index": 18,
              "bbox": [
                0.545,
                0.378,
                0.874,
                0.504
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_chart_18.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "chart_caption",
              "index": 19,
              "bbox": [
                0.503,
                0.522,
                0.91,
                0.553
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Figure 1: Validation loss during training of the big model."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.503,
            0.581,
            0.911,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in Table 1. Our model reaches 28.4 BLEU, outperforming the best previous result by 2.0 points while costing only "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3.3\\times 10^{18}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " FLOPs. Figure 1 shows that the validation loss decreases monotonically. The improvement is statistically significant "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(p <   0.05)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , although it may not generalize to low-resource pairs, as discussed in Section 2."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.502,
            0.675,
            0.912,
            0.934
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Long paragraph to cross columns. The encoder is composed of a stack of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "N = 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " identical layers. Each layer has two sub-layers: the first is a multi-head self-attention mechanism, and the second is a simple, position-wise fully connected feed-forward network with inner dimension "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "d_{ff} = 2048"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We employ a residual connection around each of the two sub-layers, followed by layer normalization [3]. That is, the output of each sub-layer is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\operatorname{LayerNorm}(x + \\operatorname{Sublayer}(x))"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . To facilitate these residual connections, all sub-layers in the model, as well as the embedding layers, produce outputs of dimension "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "d_{model} = 512"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . The decoder is also composed of a stack of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "N = 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " identical layers, and we modify the self-attention sub-layer to prevent positions from attending to subsequent positions; this masking ensures that predictions for position i can depend only on the known outputs at positions less than i."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_footnote",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.881,
            0.376,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "∗University of Example, alice@example.edu"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_footnote",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.895,
            0.328,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "†Example Labs, bob@example.com"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_footnote",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.088,
            0.906,
            0.495,
            0.932
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We found warmup essential; without it training diverged in 3 of 5 runs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 25,
